From ea59223f9d1872fcb522dfca6d67975c857ba9f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:25:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: sparx5: size the leak period from the 17-bit rate field
Organization: Wires

A credit-based shaper on a LAN969x queue lets three times its idle
slope through.  The leak period of the chip's slowest leak group,
655 Mbit/s, comes out as 400 us, which does not fit the 18-bit
LEAK_TIME field, so the group leaks every 137 us instead.

    cbs se 92: cir 0004e201 ... layer 0 timers 137856 0 0 0

The period derives from a rate maximum of 262143, but CIR_RATE is a
17-bit field.  SparX-5's groups are fast enough for the period to fit
either way.

Use the field's maximum, 131071.

Signed-off-by: Joachim Wiberg <joachim.wiberg@wires.se>
Signed-off-by: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.h
index 0f47b4ac1560..466a4b8b85ef 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/microchip/sparx5/sparx5_qos.h
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@ int sparx5_hsch_l0_get_idx(struct sparx5 *sparx5, int port, int queue);
 #define SPX5_SE_MODE_DATARATE 1
 
 /* Rate and burst */
-#define SPX5_SE_RATE_MAX 262143
+#define SPX5_SE_RATE_MAX 131071
 #define SPX5_SE_BURST_MAX 127
 #define SPX5_SE_RATE_MIN 1
 #define SPX5_SE_BURST_MIN 1
